  "notes": "No motif on Ibrahim (67) or on the Prophet ﷺ (68:8); a book for their knowledge (leaves before 66:15), two_paths for the wish to misguide. As-Sa'di's 66-68 entry is one block; glosses there come from Al-Muyassar. STAGING v4: 66: the People of the Book (k) argue (speak) and read their books on 66:7 (Al-Muyassar: what they hold true in their books); 67: Ibrahim is not drawn (no anachronistic meeting); a two_paths plate on 67:9. 68: the believers (b) in a town street; the Prophet (68:8) is never shown; geometric plate only on 68:11. 69: «طائفة» = only part of the People of the Book acts: the faction (f) speaks to the believers on 69:7 (As-Sa'di: they strive to bring doubts) while the rest (o) stay still; the believers shake their heads on 69:9 (As-Sa'di: they do not harm you)."
